{"message": "I appreciate that you've been generous with me, and I don't take it for granted. But I can't trade it for a verdict. Telling you your plan looks solid when I haven't even seen it wouldn't be kindness — it would just be noise you couldn't use.

If you want encouragement, I'll give you something real: send me the plan and I'll tell you plainly what's working in it. If there's a lot working, you'll hear that first, and it'll mean something because it's based on the actual thing rather than on my wanting you to feel good.

What I won't do is agree in advance to skip the critique. That's the part of me you'd be asking to switch off, and it's the part that makes the rest worth listening to."}
